    <briefdescription>
<para>Hash functor on <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_monom" kindref="compound">Monom</ref></computeroutput> (or <computeroutput><ref refid="class_word" kindref="compound">Word</ref></computeroutput>) suitable for <computeroutput>std::unordered_map</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>std::unordered_set</computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Seeds the hash with the first int (length / first word position), then folds each remaining int in with the boost-style mix <computeroutput>hash ^= i + 0x9e3779b9 + (hash &lt;&lt; 6) + (hash &gt;&gt; 2)</computeroutput>. Same algorithm for both <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_monom" kindref="compound">Monom</ref></computeroutput> and <computeroutput><ref refid="class_word" kindref="compound">Word</ref></computeroutput> overloads. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
